ep_13).\n\n**Temporal profile.** 1006 fires at ~[32431,32730] and ~[33331,33630], then not again until [37231,38430] and [40831,42031] (step_06, step_08). 1860 receives at ~[32431,32730], ~[33331,33630], ~[33631,34230] and ~[36631,37230] (step_07, step_09). The relay nodes 553/948 and 1390 are sparse (3\u20135 events each, step_14, step_15, step_16) and their bursts overlap the *same* buckets as 1006's own emission rather than lying strictly after it \u2014 i.e. the required strictly increasing, \u2264600\u2011gap ordering across three relay hops is not exhibited.\n\n**Confounder controls.** High volume is not the driver: 3853 events / 1895 active nodes \u2248 2 events per node, repeat_ratio 0.0026 (step_01) \u2014 an essentially non\u2011repeating background. 1860's apparent \"popularity\" comes from hub 274, which is unreachable from 1006's cluster. So neither volume nor hub popularity nor static connectivity substitutes for a time\u2011respecting chain.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_211de352\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [1006, 1860, 553, 948, 1390],\n  \"window\": [32431, 42031],\n  \"confidence\": 0.6,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_15\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_16\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"support\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"1006 and 1860 sit in separate neighbourhoods: 1860 is absent from 1006's 2-hop and 3-hop expansions, leaving only a 4-hop static route 1006->553->948->1390->1860. 1006 emits just two outgoing edges in the window and only the 553 branch is usable; the 1532 branch cannot reach 1860. The relay nodes are very sparse and their activity bursts coincide with, rather than strictly follow, 1006's emissions, so no strictly increasing chain with gaps <=600 across three relays can be established. Volume (2 events/node, repeat ratio 0.003) and 1860's apparent popularity (driven by hub 274, unreachable from 1006's cluster) are ruled out as alternative explanations. Conclusion: the static connection is real but the temporal cascade is not.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 62796, "total_output_tokens": 10486, "total_tokens": 73282, "total_latency_ms": 144939, "llm_calls": 8, "schema_repairs": 0, "tool_protocol_errors": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}